  "result": "Perfect! All 180 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/statements.js** (new module):\n   - `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that generates a customer statement\n   - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n   - Each invoice in result has: { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n   - Filters invoices:\n     - Matching customer (normalized ID)\n     - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - issueDate on or before asOf\n   - Sorts by issueDate ascending\n   - Calculates totalDue as sum of all due amounts\n   - Uses invoiceTotals() for accurate total calculation (includes VAT, discounts, vouchers)\n   - Uses balanceDue() for accurate due calculation (accounts for payments)\n   - Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customers\n   - Handles unnormalized customer IDs transparently\n\n2. **test/statements.test.js** - 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Empty statements\n   - Filtering by invoice status\n   - Date boundary conditions\n   - Customer filtering and normalization\n   - Proper sorting by issue date\n   - Due calculations with/without payments\n   - Invoice details preservation\n   - Total due aggregation\n\n**Key design**: The statement provides a point-in-time view of customer obligations, filtering for only outstanding invoices and calculating what's due based on payments already received.",
